WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.373
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:14.555
Unit eight: Adverbs of Manner. Today you will describe how actions are done.

4
00:00:14.855 --> 00:00:17.286
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:21.594
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.323
Quickly.

7
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:26.130
Quickly means in a fast way.

8
00:00:26.717 --> 00:00:27.962
He runs quickly.

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.353
Your turn. Say: Quickly.

10
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:34.992
Quickly.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.751
Slowly.

12
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.633
Slowly means in a slow way.

13
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.774
She walks slowly.

14
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:44.896
Your turn. Say: Slowly.

15
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:48.688
Slowly.

16
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.451
Carefully.

17
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.241
Carefully means with care.

18
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.048
Drive carefully.

19
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.035
Your turn. Say: Carefully.

20
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:01.750
Carefully.

21
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:03.181
Well.

22
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:05.718
Well means in a good way.

23
00:01:06.317 --> 00:01:07.504
She sings well.

24
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:10.583
Your turn. Say: Well.

25
00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:14.109
Well.

26
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:15.700
Badly.

27
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:18.658
Badly means in a bad way.

28
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.588
He slept badly.

29
00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:23.534
Your turn. Say: Badly.

30
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.331
Badly.

31
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:29.201
-ly ending.

32
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:34.004
-ly ending means the end we add to many adjectives to make adverbs.

33
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:36.245
Quick becomes quickly.

34
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.328
Your turn. Say: -ly ending.

35
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.423
-ly ending.

36
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:44.952
How.

37
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.681
How means used to ask about the way something is done.

38
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:50.389
How do you cook?

39
00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:53.299
Your turn. Say: How.

40
00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:56.833
How.

41
00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:58.387
Manner.

42
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:01.801
Manner means the way that something is done.

43
00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:04.335
Adverbs of manner say how.

44
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.138
Your turn. Say: Manner.

45
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:10.804
Manner.

46
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.914
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.018
Visal, how do you walk to school? Quickly or slowly?

48
00:02:20.117 --> 00:02:28.928
I walk quickly. Quickly is an adverb of manner. It answers the question How? and it usually comes after the verb or the object.

49
00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:31.273
How do we form them?

50
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:43.990
Add -ly to the adjective: slow, slowly; careful, carefully. If it ends in y, change y to i: happy, happily. The adverb of good is well.

51
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:46.909
Are there exceptions?

52
00:02:48.017 --> 00:02:58.198
Yes: fast, hard and late stay the same. She works hard. He drives fast. Do not say hardly, because hardly means almost not.

53
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.985
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:06.230
Grammar focus: Adverbs of manner: adjective plus -ly.

55
00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.705
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.417 --> 00:03:09.673
She walks slowly.

57
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:12.339
He speaks English well.

58
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.402
She works hard.

59
00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:23.037
Add -ly to an adjective to make an adverb of manner. Good becomes well; fast and hard do not change. Hardly means almost not.

60
00:03:23.783 --> 00:03:26.575
Be careful! Don't say: He runs quick.

61
00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:30.614
Say: He runs quickly.

62
00:03:30.914 --> 00:03:32.763
Use an adverb after the verb.

63
00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:36.440
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:38.513
Doing Things Well.

65
00:03:38.813 --> 00:03:42.032
My brother runs quickly, but my grandmother walks slowly.

66
00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.439
Please drive carefully when the road is wet.

67
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:48.990
She sings beautifully and plays the piano well.

68
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.301
He works hard, so he sleeps well.

69
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.555
The adverb answers the question: How?

70
00:03:56.667 --> 00:04:00.634
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:03.077
She drives very blank.

72
00:04:03.377 --> 00:04:07.042
A, careful. B, carefully. C, care.

73
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.774
The answer is B: carefully.

74
00:04:13.917 --> 00:04:15.626
He speaks English blank.

75
00:04:15.926 --> 00:04:19.301
A, good. B, well. C, goodly.

76
00:04:22.867 --> 00:04:24.889
The answer is B: well.

77
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.389
She works blank. (not easy)

78
00:04:28.689 --> 00:04:31.704
A, hard. B, hardly. C, hardy.

79
00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.231
The answer is A: hard.

80
00:04:38.383 --> 00:04:40.000
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.975
A, He runs quick.. B, He runs quickly.. C, He quickly runs it..

82
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:50.649
The answer is B: He runs quickly..

83
00:04:51.783 --> 00:04:54.189
According to the reading, who walks slowly?

84
00:04:54.489 --> 00:04:58.607
A, my grandmother. B, my brother. C, my mother.

85
00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.561
The answer is A: my grandmother.

86
00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:09.301
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:14.762
Write two sentences describing how you do something, using adverbs of manner.

88
00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.120
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:38.039
I study carefully before every test. I speak English slowly, so my friends understand me. In these sentences, carefully and slowly are adverbs of manner. They tell my reader how I do things.

90
00:05:38.339 --> 00:05:40.013
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:46.785
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adverbs of manner: adjective plus -ly.

92
00:05:47.085 --> 00:05:51.595
Today's value is diligence. Check the details carefully before you commit.

93
00:05:51.895 --> 00:05:54.547
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

94
00:05:54.847 --> 00:05:57.836
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

